> You can't take a monster's gloves if they're holding a weapon.

Not true. What does seem to be the case, however, is that if you only
steal one item in an attack, you steal the last item they picked up;
and since they won't pick up a cockatrice corpse unless they're
protected against it, this approach isn't going to work.

(There is a check for stoning the monster in the code, so it could
conceivably be possible to finesse your way around it in the case of,
say, chameleons or polyed monsters going from a stoning-resistant form
in which they found a rubber chicken before they found the gloves, to
a non-stoning resistant form; it's not going to help in the general
troll case, though.)

